{"base_rate":0.5076708507670851,"brier":0.1504513249651325,"bss":0.3980530211997634,"bss_hi":0.4724176739801555,"bss_lo":0.3079150180598014,"country":"ES","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.1158716875871688,"ess":359.3767948764733,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Bilbao</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Bilbao rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (98%), believe about\n<b>96%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>9%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 717 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nBILBAO AEROPUERTO, 4.2 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.40, ranked 36 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(17&ndash;59) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>9%</b></td><td class='num'>210</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>5%</td><td class='num'><b>28%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>16%</td><td class='num'><b>39%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'><b>58%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>60%</td><td class='num'><b>72%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>81%</td><td class='num'><b>86%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>98%</td><td class='num'><b>96%</b></td><td class='num'>156</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Bilbao</b> <span class=\"muted\">ES</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.40</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>17&ndash;59\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>717 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Bilbao &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Bilbao\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 75.51368421052632,343.6842105263158 114.43478260869566,292.3188405797101 179.6208219178082,217.45205479452056 268.96347826086946,123.50724637681157 346.0675,52.125 403.1953846153846,20.333333333333314 403.1953846153846,36.666666666666686 346.0675,120.375 268.96347826086946,207.91304347826087 179.6208219178082,292.24657534246575 114.43478260869566,350.47971014492754 75.51368421052632,377.2105263157895 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"197.20781032078102\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"197.20781032078102\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,349.06666666666666 75.51368421052632,281.42105263157896 114.43478260869566,239.56521739130434 179.6208219178082,172.57534246575344 268.96347826086946,118.231884057971 346.0675,69.1875 403.1953846153846,32.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 9% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 210 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"349.06666666666666\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 5%&amp;#10;It rained 28% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"75.51368421052632\" cy=\"281.42105263157896\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 16%&amp;#10;It rained 39% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"114.43478260869566\" cy=\"239.56521739130434\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 34%&amp;#10;It rained 58% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"179.6208219178082\" cy=\"172.57534246575344\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 60%&amp;#10;It rained 72% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"268.96347826086946\" cy=\"118.231884057971\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 81%&amp;#10;It rained 86% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 64 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"346.0675\" cy=\"69.1875\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 98%&amp;#10;It rained 96% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 156 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"403.1953846153846\" cy=\"32.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(51%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Bilbao the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.50) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.12).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>173</td><td class='num'>40%</td><td class='num'>0.123</td><td class='num'>16.8%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>210</td><td class='num'>53%</td><td class='num'>0.437</td><td class='num'>9.5%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>167</td><td class='num'>62%</td><td class='num'>0.459</td><td class='num'>11.7%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>167</td><td class='num'>48%</td><td class='num'>0.502</td><td class='num'>9.4%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":43.26271,"lon":-2.92528,"n":717,"n_cities":109,"name":"Bilbao","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":210,"obs":0.09047619047619047,"sig":true},{"hi":0.1,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.04947368421052631,"n":76,"obs":0.27631578947368